WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.580
- I was a government major

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:04.090
which mean I had to write a lot of papers.

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:05.590
Now when a normal student writes a paper

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:07.309
they might spread the
work out a little like.

00:00:07.309 --> 00:00:09.642
(blows air)

00:00:10.503 --> 00:00:11.950
- Man wouldn't it be nice

00:00:15.628 --> 00:00:18.342
(phone rings)

00:00:18.342 --> 00:00:19.175
hello?

00:00:19.175 --> 00:00:21.500
- [male voice on phone] Doctor Mike

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:22.929
- Yes?

00:00:22.929 --> 00:00:24.700
- [male voice on phone]
Mikhail Varshavski right?

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:25.927
- Yes, may I ask who's calling?

00:00:25.927 --> 00:00:27.776
- [male voice on phone]
Hey Mike, it's TED.

00:00:27.776 --> 00:00:29.614
- Ted who?

00:00:29.614 --> 00:00:31.990
- [male voice on phone]
TED, did I stutter?

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.930
TED conference ideas worth spreading,

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.700
talking on stages, smart people stuff.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.814
We're calling to see if you
want to do a speech with us.

00:00:38.814 --> 00:00:40.981
- (Whispers) yes yes yes yes!

00:00:40.981 --> 00:00:42.600
- [male voice on phone] Doctor Mike, Talk.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.510
- Oh yes, sorry, are you the Ted?

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:48.240
You're the guy that
started the whole thing,

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.207
you're Ted?

00:00:49.207 --> 00:00:50.626
- [male voice on phone] Good God.

00:00:50.626 --> 00:00:53.478
Hey Mike, by name is Bill I work for TED.

00:00:53.478 --> 00:00:54.840
TED is an acronym

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:58.106
it stands for Technology and
- Okay okay, say no more Bill

00:00:58.106 --> 00:01:02.283
lets make this happen, you
just name the time and place.

00:01:04.494 --> 00:01:09.231
(upbeat tropical music)

00:01:09.231 --> 00:01:14.231
(upbeat tropical music)

00:01:14.247 --> 00:01:19.247
(upbeat tropical music)

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:26.140
- Jack, Jack, hold me Jack.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:27.340
Don't let go Jack.

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:28.173
I'm just kidding.

00:01:28.173 --> 00:01:30.790
Guys we are in Monaco and
its time for my TED Talk.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:31.853
I just almost fell through the roof.

00:01:31.853 --> 00:01:35.423
(piano twinkle music)

00:01:35.423 --> 00:01:40.423
(piano twinkle music)

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:44.700
Alright so I am getting ready
to rehearse my TED Talk.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.010
There's people on stage right now,

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:49.010
you can see that they're
practicing their speeches.

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:50.480
Basically they're asking people

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.320
to do one minute of their
speech to do a sound check.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:54.800
I'm gonna do my intro

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:58.730
and because no one else even
the director of this talk

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:00.010
has heard my speech before,

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:02.398
I'm really excited to give it to them.

00:02:02.398 --> 00:02:03.810
(piano twinkle music)

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:06.371
Being such a huge fan
of the TED conference,

00:02:06.371 --> 00:02:10.288
to get a call and an invitation
to speak at a conference

00:02:10.288 --> 00:02:11.630
was just incredible.

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:14.780
I mean there's so much that I wanna say.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.800
I've been put in this unique situation

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.810
where I'm in between medicine
and marketing and YouTube

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:20.790
and all this stuff.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:23.620
